<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regulamentul Organic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a>–<a href="/years/1832">1832</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Organic Regulation, Organic Statute</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Regulamentul Organic was the quasi-constitutional law introduced in Wallachia in 1831 and Moldavia in 1832 while the principalities were under Russian occupation after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1828-1829">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1828–1829. Drafted under the Russian governor Pavel Kiselyov, it created modern ministries, budgets, a militia and assemblies dominated by the boyars, and remained the framework of government until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-convention-of-1858">Paris Convention of 1858</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/regulamentul-organic.jpg" alt="Regulamentul Organic" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wallachian_Regulamentul_organic_1832.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
